{"description":"Resolve Phase 5 checksum blocker: current p5-checksum-manifest acceptance requires Caddy SHA-512 and NSS certutil SHA-256 verification, while p5-release-ci produces only Avior CLI archives and current CLI verify checks project prerequisites rather than release binary integrity. Investigate whether scope targets dependency binaries, Avior release artifacts, or both; define artifact ownership/packaging, manifest format and algorithm mapping, generation pipeline, CLI discovery and verification lifecycle, fail-closed behavior, and authenticity boundary. Co-located checksum files provide corruption detection only, not authenticity.","investigationNotes":"","conclusion":"","acceptanceCriteria":"Document evidence and recommendation for checksum scope (Caddy/NSS dependencies vs Avior release binaries); enumerate artifacts, platform/version naming, manifest schema/encoding and generation owner; specify verifier entry point, trust/distribution source, fail-closed cases and tests; assess whether checksum alone meets H3 security intent or requires signed manifest/independent trust root; identify planning changes needed to p5-checksum-manifest and p5-release-ci, including whether to split items. Publish decision/recommended revised acceptance criteria; no implementation required.","decisionCriteria":["Traceable to approved H3 intent and Phase 5 scope","No false claim that unsigned co-located checksums authenticate artifacts","Deterministic, fail-closed verifier contract with testable failure cases","Clear division between release pipeline artifact generation and CLI verification","Minimum planning changes needed to remove acceptance ambiguity"],"researchQuestions":["What exact H3 finding and security property must checksum verification provide?","Which artifacts are built, downloaded, cached, or installed by Avior on each supported OS?","Should release checksums cover Avior binaries/archives, Caddy, NSS certutil, or all?","What stable manifest format, algorithm labels, filenames, version/platform identifiers and encoding should be used?","Where does CLI obtain manifest and artifact; when does verification run; what happens on missing, malformed, unknown algorithm, or mismatch?","Is integrity against accidental corruption sufficient, or must authenticity resist replacement of both artifact and manifest?","Which plan items and CI ownership change after recommendation?"]}